"about": "The tractus of the formulary “Third Sunday of Lent” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "To You I have lifted up my eyes, who dwell in heaven. Behold, as the eyes of servants are on the hands of their masters, and as the eyes of the handmaid are on the hands of her mistress, so are our eyes toward the Lord our God, until He has mercy on us. Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w004", "w005"], "anchor": "w004", "gloss": "my eyes" }, { "words": ["w016", "w017"], "anchor": "w016", "gloss": "of their masters" }, { "words": ["w024", "w025"], "anchor": "w024", "gloss": "of her mistress" }, { "words": ["w027", "w028"], "anchor": "w027", "gloss": "our eyes" }, { "words": ["w031", "w032"], "anchor": "w031", "gloss": "our God" }] }
  "w006": { "gloss": "who" },

"about": "The epistola of the formulary “13th Sunday after Pentecost” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: The promises were spoken to Abraham and to his seed. He does not say: And to seeds, as referring to many, but as referring to one: And to your seed, who is Christ. Now this I say: the law, which came into being four hundred and thirty years afterward, does not so annul the testament confirmed by God as to cancel the promise. For if the inheritance comes from the law, then it no longer comes from the promise. But to Abraham God granted it by promise. What, then, is the law? It was laid down because of transgressions, until the seed should come to whom He had made the promise, ordained through angels by the hand of a mediator. Now a mediator is not of one; God, however, is one. So is the law against the promises of God? Far from it. For if there had been given a law able to give life, justice would indeed come from the law. But Scripture has confined all things under sin, so that the promise might be granted, from the faith of Jesus Christ, to those who believe.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w003", "w004"], "anchor": "w003", "gloss": "were spoken" }, { "words": ["w021", "w022"], "anchor": "w021", "gloss": "to your seed" }, { "words": ["w039", "w040"], "anchor": "w039", "gloss": "came into being" }, { "words": ["w068", "w069"], "anchor": "w068", "gloss": "it was enacted" }, { "words": ["w083", "w084", "w085"], "anchor": "w085", "gloss": "is not of one" }, { "words": ["w096", "w097"], "anchor": "w096", "gloss": "For if" }, { "words": ["w098", "w099"], "anchor": "w098", "gloss": "had been given" }] }
  "w075": { "gloss": "ordained" },

"about": "The epistola of the formulary “19th Sunday after Pentecost” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: Be renewed in the spirit of your mind, and put on the new man, who has been created according to God in justice and holiness of truth. For this reason, putting away lying, let each of you speak the truth with his neighbor, for we are members of one another. Be angry, yet do not sin; let the sun not go down on your anger. Do not make room for the devil. Whoever used to steal, let him steal no longer; but rather let him labor, working with his own hands at what is good, so that he may have something to give to a person in need.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w004", "w005"], "anchor": "w004", "gloss": "of your mind" }, { "words": ["w013", "w014"], "anchor": "w013", "gloss": "has been created" }, { "words": ["w028", "w029"], "anchor": "w028", "gloss": "his own neighbor" }, { "words": ["w039", "w040"], "anchor": "w040", "gloss": "let not go down" }, { "words": ["w042", "w043"], "anchor": "w042", "gloss": "your anger" }, { "words": ["w051", "w052"], "anchor": "w052", "gloss": "let not steal" }, { "words": ["w057", "w058"], "anchor": "w057", "gloss": "with his own hands" }] }
  "w066": { "gloss": "need" },
  "w067": { "gloss": "to one suffering" }

"about": "The epistola of the formulary “16th Sunday after Pentecost” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: I entreat you not to falter in my tribulations for you, which is your glory. On this account I bend my knees before the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, from whom every fatherhood in the heavens and on earth is named, that He may give you, according to the riches of His glory, to be strengthened with might through His Spirit for the inner man, and that Christ may dwell by faith in your hearts; in order that you, rooted and founded in love, may be able to grasp what the breadth and the length and the loftiness and the depth are, together with all the saints, and to know also the love of Christ which surpasses knowledge, so that you may be filled to the whole fullness of God. And to Him who can do all things far more abundantly than we ask or understand, according to the power that works within us, to Him be glory within the Church and in Christ Jesus, to all generations, forever and ever. Amen.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w007", "w008"], "anchor": "w007", "gloss": "my tribulations" }, { "words": ["w013", "w014"], "anchor": "w013", "gloss": "your glory" }, { "words": ["w016", "w017"], "anchor": "w016", "gloss": "for this reason" }, { "words": ["w019", "w020"], "anchor": "w019", "gloss": "my knees" }, { "words": ["w023", "w024"], "anchor": "w023", "gloss": "of our Lord" }, { "words": ["w042", "w043"], "anchor": "w042", "gloss": "of His glory" }, { "words": ["w057", "w058"], "anchor": "w057", "gloss": "your hearts" }] }
  "w015": { "gloss": "For this" },

"about": "The epistola of the formulary “Saint Matthias the Apostle” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "In those days, Peter, standing up among the brethren — now there was a crowd of people together, about one hundred twenty — said: Men, brethren, it is necessary that the Scripture be fulfilled which was spoken beforehand by the Holy Spirit through the mouth of David about Judas, who was the leader of those who seized Jesus; who had been counted among us, and received the lot of this ministry. And this man indeed possessed a field from the reward of iniquity, and, having been hanged, burst open in the middle, and all his entrails were poured out. And this became known to all who lived in Jerusalem, so that that field was called in their tongue Aceldama, which means, the field of blood. In the book of Psalms, indeed, it is written: Let their abode become deserted, and let there be no one to dwell in it; and let another take his bishopric. It is necessary, then, that from these men who have assembled with us all the time in which the Lord Jesus went in and out among us, beginning from the baptism of John until the day on which He was taken up from us, one of these become with us a witness of His resurrection. So they proposed two: Joseph, who was called Barsabas, who bore the surname Justus, and Matthias. And praying, they said: Lord, You who know every heart, make known which one You have chosen of these two to receive the place of this ministry and of the apostleship, from which Judas turned aside through transgression, to depart to his own place. Then they gave them lots, and the lot fell on Matthias, and he was counted with the eleven apostles.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w002", "w003"], "anchor": "w002", "gloss": "those days" }, { "words": ["w025", "w026"], "anchor": "w025", "gloss": "the Holy Spirit" }, { "words": ["w040", "w041"], "anchor": "w040", "gloss": "had been numbered" }, { "words": ["w045", "w046"], "anchor": "w045", "gloss": "was allotted" }, { "words": ["w063", "w064"], "anchor": "w063", "gloss": "gushed out" }, { "words": ["w070", "w071"], "anchor": "w070", "gloss": "became" }, { "words": ["w087", "w088", "w089"], "anchor": "w087", "gloss": "For it is written" }, { "words": ["w098", "w099"], "anchor": "w099", "gloss": "let there not be" }, { "words": ["w116", "w117"], "anchor": "w117", "gloss": "were together" }, { "words": ["w133", "w134"], "anchor": "w134", "gloss": "until" }, { "words": ["w137", "w138"], "anchor": "w137", "gloss": "was taken up" }, { "words": ["w157", "w158"], "anchor": "w157", "gloss": "was surnamed" }, { "words": ["w186", "w187"], "anchor": "w186", "gloss": "fell away" }, { "words": ["w192", "w193"], "anchor": "w192", "gloss": "his place" }, { "words": ["w204", "w205"], "anchor": "w204", "gloss": "was numbered" }] }
  "w039": { "gloss": "who" },

"about": "The graduale of the formulary “Seven Sorrows of the Blessed Virgin Mary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "You are sorrowful and tearful, O Virgin Mary, standing beside the Cross of your Son, the Lord Jesus, the Redeemer. O Virgin Mother of God, the One whom all the world does not contain, the author of life become man, bears this torment of the Cross.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w012", "w013"], "anchor": "w012", "gloss": "your Son" }, { "words": ["w019", "w020", "w021", "w022"], "anchor": "w021", "gloss": "the whole world does not contain" }] }
  "w004": { "gloss": "are" },

"about": "The graduale of the formulary “Visitation of the Blessed Virgin Mary” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "s01": { "translation": "You are blessed and venerable, O Virgin Mary, who were found to be the Savior’s mother with your chastity untouched. O Virgin Mother of God, the One whom all the world does not contain, become man, enclosed Himself within your womb.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w011", "w012"], "anchor": "w011", "gloss": "were found" }, { "words": ["w019", "w020", "w021", "w022"], "anchor": "w021", "gloss": "the whole world does not contain" }] }
